# Line endings are release-managed by the builder, not by git: it rewrites the
# Windows launchers (*.cmd, *.ps1) to CRLF in every release artifact -- macOS
# and Windows alike -- and leaves everything else, including *.sh and
# *.command, as LF. Disabling git text conversion keeps checkouts on every
# platform byte-identical to what shipped, so those CRLF launchers stay CRLF,
# the LF shell scripts stay LF, and the signed release marker
# (.community-release.json) keeps verifying.
* -text
*.cmd whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.ps1 whitespace=cr-at-eol
